 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Not necessarily, many people do it without incident. A dry bike is much better than a wet one, so always wipe it down after every ride. Yes, a light blanket over them. Hands get cold too, a thin pair of gloves under a thin layer keeps them happy. That's the way to do it. Snow days are always fun, bike trips less so. Not necessarily, regular tires do fine, it's the stops that take toll. Lots of shelter and hot drinks in between help too.",
